      "message": "feat(turning): threading option to repeat each roughing depth\n\nA Threading op's infeed plan gains \"repeat each depth\" (default off):\nevery roughing pass above the root is followed by an identical copy of\nitself - same tip, same lattice shift, same helix phase - before the\nladder steps deeper (\"spring at each depth\"). The finishing and spring\npasses at the root are not repeated; alternating infeed counts depths,\nnot cuts, so a repeat keeps its flank. The verdict judges the laid\npasses, repeats included, and stays clean.\n\nG32 passes only: the thread-cycle record carries a repeat_each_depth\nflag (`REP 1` in the stream, property RepeatEachDepth, cache key only\nwhen set) and fanuc-lathe's G76 refuses it by name. Defaults are\nbyte-identical: no extra stamp byte, no project key, no stream word,\nno golden moved. UI: a \"Repeat each depth\" checkbox on the Passes tab,\nits tooltip noting tooling makers recommend against routine spring\npasses.\n\nFixes #418\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
