      "message": "feat(turning): in-pass chip-break dips inside a continuous G32 chain\n\nA Threading op's infeed plan gains chip-break dips (interval, radial\nheight, length; interval 0 = off, the default). Each roughing pass lifts\nradially and returns a few times along the thread, inside its one\nsynchronized chain: a dip is a variable-radius thread half-turn (same\nhalf lead of axial travel, the radius ramping out or back), so the\nstation every spindle angle meets - the helix phase - is the plain\npass's. Never deeper than the pass (a radial lift on the pass's own\nstation stands inside its V), ramps kept under 45 degrees (diameter\nchange below axial travel), never in the first or last lead, never on\nthe finishing, spring or repeat passes, height at most every dipped\npass's depth of cut. Refused by name otherwise.\n\nPosting: fanuc-lathe declares continuousThreading = true, citing FANUC\nB-64304EN-1 sections 3.4 (continuous threading keeps spindle sync at\nblock joints) and 3.2 (WARNING 6: a threading block after a threading\nblock starts without waiting for the one-rotation signal; G32 tapers,\nF the Z lead up to 45 degrees), and writes each dip as G32 X Z F,\nrefusing a segment that does not continue a G32 chain, is steeper than\n45 degrees or deeper than its plunge. The record carries\nchip_break_dips (DIP 1, ChipBreakDips, cache key only when set); the\nsection carries PARAM ChipBreakDips, which the engine refuses by name\nfor a script without the flag; G76 refuses dips by name. The thread\nverdict re-reads every chain for the phase, depth, slope and placement\nlaws and convicts a breach as a gouge (holds the post).\n\nDefaults byte-identical: no stamp byte, project key, stream word or\nPARAM; no golden moved. New golden thread_g32_dips.nc. UI: dip rows on\nthe Passes tab.\n\nFixes #419\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
